  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Policy and Systems Research to tackle low vaccine acceptance in low- and middle-income countries (LMICs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A collaboration between the World Health Organization (WHO) Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research (AHPSR) and the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) to support a call for Health Policy and Systems research proposals tackling the issue of low vaccine acceptance in low- and middle-income countries (LMIC).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve the understanding of factors underlying low vaccine acceptance through formative and contextual analysis of supply- and demand-side constraints, including around the social determinants of health;&#x202f;&#x202f; 
Support the development of cutting-edge Health Policy and Systems Research (HPSR) that uses a variety of methods and approaches, including but not limited to participatory action research and ethnography to identify potential strategies to address low vaccine acceptance as well as appropriate methodologies (including the use of mixed methods approaches) to examine the implementation of these strategies in particular national/sub-national contexts; and&#x202f; 
Engage with governments at national and sub-national levels and with civil society to examine how learning can inform the development of programmes and policies to address challenges around vaccine acceptance.</narrative>
  </description>
